The [code-snippets design brief](/lore/code-snippets) requires whole-file tokenization.
The highlighter receives the full source before the pipeline selects lines.
Shiki exposes [`codeToTokens`](https://shiki.style/guide/install) for token output.

An excerpt can start inside a multiline comment or string.
Tokenizing only the excerpt removes the preceding source from the highlighter's input.

The proposed pipeline:
1. Tokenizes every source line.
2. Selects the requested ranges.
3. Keeps the original line numbers.
4. Inserts a collapsed gap between separated ranges.

A collapsed gap labels omitted lines separately from source lines.

The planned property compares excerpt tokens with the same lines from whole-file tokenization.
It includes multiline comments and template strings.
See [property-based testing](/lore/property-based-testing).

Both renderers consume [one snippet model](/lore/one-snippet-model-two-renderers).
See [the glossary](/glossary) for whole-file tokenization and collapsed gap.
